==Strategy==
The main rule here is to get as many treasures ([[Aqua Crystal|Aqua]]/[[Plasma Crystal]]) as possible before attempting this stage. This matters the most in the third chapter. Although you could beat the moons without all treasures, you'll need them eventually as Unstarred Aliens can appear far beyond Into The Future.

==='''Chapter 1'''===
It is wise to ignore the time reward on your first try, as this stage will become an absolute joke with the treasures from future chapters. Do note that if you happen to own [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Fish Cat]], then this stage also becomes an absolute joke, regardless of your treasures, allowing beginners to get timed score rewards on their very first attempt at this stage. [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Rover]], [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pole Vaulter]], [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Medalist]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly]], [[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Saw]], and most [[Crazed Cats (origin)|Crazed Cats]] are all very good in this stage and recommended if you have them.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Note that having all treasures matters even more than in the previous stage, so, if you are struggling, go and get them all (Aqua and Plasma Crystals from both Ch. 1 and 2). Ranged attackers that don't use much cash and preferably have >350 range are very useful here. Try ranged single target attackers ([[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon]], [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sexy Bathtub Cat]], ...) with ranged area units ([[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]], ...). When approaching the base, wait a bit before sending out your fast meatshields as they will stack up and quickly clog the cat limit, creating a hole in your defense.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
You should have most of the Crazed Cats and all the True Forms of Normal Cats by now. Use a bunch of meatshields and bring stuff like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Legs]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon]], [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Holy Valkyrie]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut]] and [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] (if you don't have Ururun, use another meatshield), then you shouldn't have trouble. This stage becomes substantially easier as Raging Bahamut has an easy to exploit semi-long attack animation, giving time for your meatshields to take place before another hit takes place. Ubers from [[Nature's Guardians ELEMENTAL PIXIES (Gacha Event)|Elemental Pixies]], [[Justice Strikes Back! Dark Heroes (Gacha Event)|Dark Heroes]] and [[The Almighties The Majestic Zeus (Gacha Event)|The Almighties]] work well here or any decent anti alien Ubers like [[Terun (Uber Rare Cat)|Terun]] works well.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] - Corrupted Psychocat's [[Slow]] ability can help immensely when stacked to great amounts.
*[[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] - Thanks to their great range, they will help in chipping down Raging Bahamut Cat.
*[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] - Crazed Sexy Legs can chip down Raging Bahamut at a relatively safe distance, their [[Wave Attack]]s are also useful for the peons.
*[[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] - Ururun Cat outranges Raging Bahamut and also knock him back occasionally to gain ground.

